Suggestion 1. Adjust the for loop range to include the last character. Change the for loop condition from `for (int i = 1; i < s.length() - 1; i++)` to `for (int i = 1; i < s.length(); i++)`. This ensures that the loop checks every character from the second to the last one.
```java
for (int i = 1; i < s.length(); i++) {
    if (!s.substring(i, i + 1).matches("[a-z]")) {
        System.out.println("No");
        return;
    }
}
```

fix_code:
public static void main(String[] args) {
    try (Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in)) {
        String s = sc.next();
        if (!s.substring(0, 1).matches("[A-Z]")) {
            System.out.println("No");
            return;
        }
        for (int i = 1; i < s.length(); i++) { // adjusted loop range to include the last character
            if (!s.substring(i, i + 1).matches("[a-z]")) {
                System.out.println("No");
                return;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Yes");
    }
}
